  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 405 PM EDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nThe SPC has introduced a Marginal risk for severe weather on Monday. \nThe main risk will be south of a line from Columbus to Macon as a \ncold front moves in. A surge of warm moist air will push in from the \ngulf under SW flow with the GFS indicating the potential for 2000+ \nJ/KG of CAPE during the afternoon. Bulk shear values appear to be on \nthe marginal side as the front comes through, but given the dynamics \nit would appear that the potential for a few strong storms during \nthe afternoon is likely. \n\nRain should clear the area Monday night and high pressure will \nsettle in behind it. Cooler conditions will linger through next \nWednesday with highs in the mid 70s with lows in the mid 40s and low \n50s. Temps will heat up late next week as temps climb back into the \nlow to mid 80s. The rest of the week should be rain free, as the \nridge continues to build.",
